.TH snip-init 1  "snip 0.6.0" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-init \- create and import snippet libraries
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip init\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-git\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
\fBsnip import\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip import snippetslab\fR <\fB\-\-into\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Create a new .sniplib library or import an existing SnippetsLab collection. init can create a dedicated Git repository and record a human\-readable library name. In noninteractive use, pass an explicit path or \-\-yes.
.PP
SnippetsLab imports require a destination library. Run with \-\-dry\-run first to inspect counts, normalized tags, attachments, and validation warnings without modifying the destination.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip init"
.PP
Create a new filesystem snippet library
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Human\-readable library name
.TP
\fB\-\-git\fR
Initialize a dedicated Git repository after creating the library
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the interactive setup and use defaults
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Directory to create. Defaults to an interactive or platform\-specific choice
.SS "snip import"
.PP
Import another snippet format
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip import snippetslab"
.PP
Import a SnippetsLab library or export
.TP
\fB\-\-into\fR \fI<INTO>\fR
Destination snip library
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Validate and report the import without writing it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>
SnippetsLab source file or directory
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Create a Git\-backed library without prompting:
.RS 4
.nf
snip init ~/Notes.sniplib \-\-name Notes \-\-git \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview and then perform a SnippetsLab import:
.RS 4
.nf
snip import snippetslab SnippetsLab.json \-\-into ~/Imported.sniplib \-\-dry\-run
snip import snippetslab SnippetsLab.json \-\-into ~/Imported.sniplib
.fi
.RE
